      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"step-q89479\" class=\"step questionWidget\" style=\"display: block;\"><div class=\"questionWidget-header\"><div class=\"questionWidget-title\">Question 5</div><div class=\"questionWidget-helpButton\">?</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-text\"><p>Which of the following random variables follow a geometric distribution?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  The number of victories by a chess player in 10 matches </li><li>  The number of arrows fired by an archer before hitting the bullseye </li><li>  The number of students that pass a calculus exam among a group of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"9\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> students </li></ol></div><table class=\"questionWidget-choicesTable\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-89479-a\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\" style=\"background: rgb(64, 64, 64); color: white;\">a</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">II only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-89479-b\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">b</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and III only\n</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-89479-c\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">c</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and II only\n</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-89479-d\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">d</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-89479-e\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">e</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">III only</td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>A geometric distribution is used to model the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.</p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Random variable I does <em>not</em> follow a geometric distribution. Winning a chess game is a binomial experiment, but the number of times the player wins cannot be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Random variable II follows a geometric distribution. Firing an arrow is a binomial experiment, and the number of arrows fired before the first arrow hits the bullseye can be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Random variable III does <em>not</em> follow a geometric distribution. Passing a calculus exam is a binomial experiment, but the number of students passing the exam cannot be interpreted as the number of binomial experiments needed before the first success.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
