    "q-130665": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130665",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "At a fruit store, every basket with $40$ apples has $2$ rotten apples, on average. If an employee checks only one apple from each basket, what is the probability that they will find the first rotten apple on the $7$th basket they check? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of baskets checked until a rotten apple is found. On average, the chance of finding a rotten apple is \n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{40}=0.05.\n$$\n\nSo, the number of baskets that the employee checks before finding a rotten apple can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success $p=0.05.$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.05).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.05)^{x-1}(0.05) \\\\  & =(0.95)^{x-1}(0.05)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding the first rotten apple on the $7$th basket is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =f(7) \\\\  & =(0.95)^{7-1}(0.05) \\\\  & =(0.95)^{6}(0.05) \\\\  & ≈0.037\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
