    "q-130952": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130952",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Every week at a restaurant $2$ out of $100$ plates, on average, get a little breakage and are replaced at the end of the week. If the manager is checking the plates at the end of a certain week, what is the probability that they will check more than $4$ plates before finding a broken one? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of plates checked until a broken one is found. On average, the chance of finding a broken plate is \n\n$$\np=\\frac{2}{100}=0.02.\n$$\n\nSo, the number of plates that the manager checks before finding a broken one can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success $p=0.02.$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.02).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.02)^{x-1}(0.02) \\\\  & =(0.98)^{x-1}(0.02)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute $P(X>4),$ we will use the complement:\n\n$$\nP(X>4)=1-P(X\\le 4)\n$$\n\nComputing the probability of the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 4) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.98)^{1-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{2-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{3-1}(0.02)+(0.98)^{4-1}(0.02) \\\\  & =(0.02)+(0.98)(0.02)+(0.98)^{2}(0.02)+(0.98)^{3}(0.02) \\\\  & =[1+0.98+(0.98)^{2}+(0.98)^{3}](0.02) \\\\  & ≈0.078\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the probability of checking more than $4$ plates before finding a broken one is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & ≈1-0.078 \\\\  & =0.922\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
